            "subject": "Cover the candidate deck with e2e specs",
            "body": "Cover the candidate deck with e2e specs\n\nSix specs over the button path: the header chip, the opened deck, advancing and\nundoing, the auto-submit payload, and the empty state. They drive the ✕ / ✓\nbuttons rather than the swipe — Reanimated gestures do not survive the Expo web\nexport, and the buttons are the accessible path that has to work anyway. The\ngesture itself stays a manual check on a simulator.\n\nThe payload spec is the one that matters: it asserts which ids land in\naccepted_ids and rejected_ids, which is the same class of defect that once sent\nevery candidate to the reject list on web.\n\nVerified by breaking the auto-submit condition and watching that spec fail, then\nrestoring it.\n\nAlso follows the API's move to a paginated candidates list: the header chip now\ncounts total_items across pages rather than the length of the current one.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n",
            "author": {
